(4780856, 689017, 94073, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tpbremer:</b></div><hr/><i> I think you really border on offensive when you post a picture of a stabbed pregnant woman.  It doesn''t offend me, but I do think its pretty gross.  I also think you might be getting killed in your score.  I think others in this challenge achieved a more real grim feeling with a less is more attitude. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not to be rude, I really appreciate your comments...but crime scenes are generally OFFENSIVE. If they weren''t...they wouldn''t be CRIME SCENES. Dont believe me? Look up the real crime scene photos from the murders that inspired IN COLD BLOOD. <br/> <br/>:)<br/> <br/>But I can honestly see where you are coming from. Thanks for the tip!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-23 00:35:55.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by tpbremer: I think you really border on offensive when you post a picture of a stabbed pregnant woman.  It doesn''t offend me, but I do think its pretty gross.  I also think you might be getting killed in your score.  I think others in this challenge achieved a more real grim feeling with a less is more attitude.   Not to be rude, I really appreciate your comments...but crime scenes are generally OFFENSIVE. If they weren''t...they wouldn''t be CRIME SCENES. Dont believe me? Look up the real crime scene photos from the murders that inspired IN COLD BLOOD.  :) But I can honestly see where you are coming from. Thanks for the tip!', '2008-06-23 01:34:48.000000', '2008-06-23 01:35:55.000000', 0),
(4780858, 688857, 69102, '<td valign="top">Fantastically realized. Should have placed much higher. For the idiot who said this isn''t noir [because it had too much color] - it is best to remain silent and be thought a fool, than to open one''s mouth and remove all doubt. Look up "Vertigo," or even better Elliot Gould''s, "The Long Goodbye" for examples of the noir style done exceptionally well, in color.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-24 16:01:49.</i></td>', 'Fantastically realized. Should have placed much higher. For the idiot who said this isn''t noir [because it had too much color] - it is best to remain silent and be thought a fool, than to open one''s mouth and remove all doubt. Look up "Vertigo," or even better Elliot Gould''s, "The Long Goodbye" for examples of the noir style done exceptionally well, in color.', '2008-06-23 01:36:05.000000', '2008-06-24 17:01:49.000000', 0),
(4780859, 689043, 53814, '<td valign="top">Great job capturing a senseless and heinous crime scene, and in Tranquility, no less.</td>', 'Great job capturing a senseless and heinous crime scene, and in Tranquility, no less.', '2008-06-23 01:36:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4780861, 689017, 94073, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by metatate:</b></div><hr/><i> kinda goofy - 2 knives?  My wife is 7 months pregnant so I might be biased. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah. We thought about going for only one. But towards the end of the shoot...I started thinking of this crime more as a suicide and less as a murder. Two knives would make sense in that case...because she wants to make sure both of them die.<br/> <br/>Anyways..didn''t work. Back to the drawing board!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by metatate: kinda goofy - 2 knives?  My wife is 7 months pregnant so I might be biased.   Yeah. We thought about going for only one. But towards the end of the shoot...I started thinking of this crime more as a suicide and less as a murder. Two knives would make sense in that case...because she wants to make sure both of them die. Anyways..didn''t work. Back to the drawing board! Thanks for the comment.', '2008-06-23 01:37:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4780863, 689017, 94073, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Patsfan:</b></div><hr/><i> Strange shot and you can tell it''s not blood. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL. Yeah. I didn''t have time to make ''fake blood''. I didn''t even think of my idea until about two hours before submission time. I was eating a watermelon..when the idea STABBED me.  :D</td>', 'Originally posted by Patsfan: Strange shot and you can tell it''s not blood.   LOL. Yeah. I didn''t have time to make ''fake blood''. I didn''t even think of my idea until about two hours before submission time. I was eating a watermelon..when the idea STABBED me.  :D', '2008-06-23 01:38:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4780864, 689060, 30861, '<td valign="top">I actually believe the processing on the one you entered is MUCH better for the challenge than the alternate version you linked. It is grainier, grungier, more surreal in every way. MUCH better. So much better I wonder if the other version still would have ribboned. <br/> <br/>Why not start a thread about it (say at the start I asked you to) and ask people THEIR opinions. Be really interesting to see what the consensus is...<br/> <br/>Nice work!</td>', 'I actually believe the processing on the one you entered is MUCH better for the challenge than the alternate version you linked. It is grainier, grungier, more surreal in every way. MUCH better. So much better I wonder if the other version still would have ribboned.  Why not start a thread about it (say at the start I asked you to) and ask people THEIR opinions. Be really interesting to see what the consensus is... Nice work!', '2008-06-23 01:38:41.000000', NULL, 0),
